@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 11, 17 and 16 corrections"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.20.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage/1.20.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1617corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.20.0 (2026-11-20): Owner note on the queued lab package recorded: its content is to be drawn from the book's resources on GitHub, not written ad hoc. Earlier: routing of a new instruction recorded: the lab-materials package is queued as the next lineage (route c), not started. The lineage stays open."@en .

ex:Lineage10 backlog:hasAuditNote "Owner note 2026-11-20 (11:04): the lab content is to be discussed with the owner before any work, and must use the book's resources where they are available on GitHub (the 3rd-edition book ontology package and this repository's textbook and assessment records) rather than ad hoc material. Recorded against the queued lab lineage; nothing written for it." .
ex:Lineage10 backlog:hasAuditNote "Routing 2026-11-20 (G195): the owner asked for a lab-materials package (lab handouts, quizzes with answers, one interactive HTML page per session, reusable by any Python course; repository to follow). It does not serve this lineage's mission and is not urgent, so route (c): queued as the next lineage, opened only after this lineage is concluded and the owner confirms; no file of the package was written. The owner chose this route over closing this lineage as partial or declaring an urgency." .
